# Input
```graphql
# should generate diagnostics
type SomeObject {
	foo: String
	bar: String
	foo: String
}

interface SomeInterface {
	foo: String
	bar: String
	foo: String
}

input SomeInputObject {
	foo: String
	bar: String
	foo: String
}

extend type SomeObject {
	foo: String
	bar: String
	foo: String
}

extend interface SomeInterface {
	foo: String
	bar: String
	foo: String
}

extend input SomeInputObject {
	foo: String
	bar: String
	foo: String
}

type TwoDuplicates {
	foo: String
	bar: String
	foo: String
	bar: String
}

```

# Diagnostics
```
invalid.graphql:3:2 lint/correctness/noDuplicateFieldDefinitionNames ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  × The field name "foo" is used more than once.
  
    1 │ # should generate diagnostics
    2 │ type SomeObject {
  > 3 │ 	foo: String
      │ 	^^^
    4 │ 	bar: String
    5 │ 	foo: String
  
  i The field "foo" is repeated here.
  
    3 │ 	foo: String
    4 │ 	bar: String
  > 5 │ 	foo: String
      │ 	^^^
    6 │ }
    7 │ 
  
  i A GraphQL complex type is only valid if all its fields are uniquely named. Make sure to name every field differently.
  

